TI  - Development pattern of pasture livestock in arid mountains of Northwest China with a case of Sunan County
T2  - IGARSS 2005: IEEE International Geoscience and Remote Sensing Symposium, Vols 1-8, Proceedings
CP  - 25th IEEE International Geoscience and Remote Sensing Symposium (IGARSS 2005)
AB  - Grassland degradation in arid mountain areas of Northwest China mostly attributes to its backward economic situation and mismanagement. In this paper, with Sunan County in Qilian Mountains its a case study, a pasture livestock development pattern has been developed. According to this pattern, the Qilian Mountain areas and its ice-melt water irrigated oasis were regarded its it holistic coupling system. The development pattern has been divided into two sub-patterns, namely grassland management pattern, and animal production pattern. In grassland management pattern, the degraded grassland can be restored step by step by contracting grassland with households and restrictinu livestock numbers accordina to pasture carrying capacity. In animal production pattern, mountain pasture system and oasis farming system can be coupled together by developing livestock propagation in mountains and fattening in oasis. As a result, household incomes in mountain pasture area can be increased 2.5-3 times and oasis-farming, area can be increased 2-5 times. The development pattern will be beneficial to increase the households' income, lighten grazing pressure, alleviate pasture degradation, and finally realize sustainable development in the arid mountain areas.
