TI  - A solution to web-based remote sensing data access and analysis
T2  - IGARSS 2005: IEEE International Geoscience and Remote Sensing Symposium, Vols 1-8, Proceedings
CP  - 25th IEEE International Geoscience and Remote Sensing Symposium (IGARSS 2005)
AB  - In this paper, we discussed the techniques of accessing and analyzing remotely sensed data stored in internet/intranet servers from client browsers. First, the existing approaches for web-based image sharing are compared. Then, to overcome the limitations of present methods, we introduce a new architecture which integrates ION (IDL on Net) and ARCIMS in developing data servers-processing the image data stored in database and/or in files. Some operations, such as online enhancement, classification and filtering, which cannot he implemented before, can now he easily achieved, although this is somewhat time-consuming in some cases. Finally, we set up our national Landsat-7 ETM Plus imagery database by intearating ION with ARCIMS, and desirable results were obtained.
